    "summary_observations": [
      "CORRECTION (2026-08-10, qou-okxx): the writhe is now computed from the braid word.  The fourth row previously carried a hardcoded writhe of 4 for a word whose writhe is +2, which made its a_K = 1 + w\u00b7\u27e8c\u27e9\u00b7h twice too large.",
      "CORRECTION (2026-08-10, qou-okxx): three rows were mislabelled. \u03c3_1^3 in B_3 closes to the SPLIT LINK 3_1 \u2294 0_1 (2 components, Alexander \u2261 0, det 0), not the trefoil \u2014 the trefoil is a knot and sits at braid index 2.  (\u03c3_1 \u03c3_2)^3 closes to the TORUS LINK T(3,3) (3 components, det 4), not a 'toral form of 3_1'. \u03c3_1^2 \u03c3_2^-1 \u03c3_1^2 \u03c3_2^-1 closes to a 3-component link of determinant 12, so it is neither 5_2 (a knot, det 7) nor any knot.  Component counts are computed from the underlying permutation; determinants are |\u0394(\u22121)| via the reduced Burau representation.",
      "LEVEL (2026-08-10): the writhe is Markov-I invariant but shifts by \u00b11 under Markov II, so every row records its n_strands and whether it sits at the braid index of its own closure.  Only the T(3,3) row does (braid index 3).  Per the owner ruling in docs/audits/2026-08-10-writhe-level-of-definition.md the observable is evaluated at the lowest level of the tower, so the two \u03c3_1^{\u00b13} rows are OFF-LEVEL diagnostics: the minimal-level trefoil datum is the H_2 row of the companion chirality_avg_content.py.",
      "The two \u03c3_1^{\u00b13} rows give \u27e8c\u27e9_\u03b2 = \u00b11.815, antisymmetric under the braid mirror as required.  This is a statement about the braid words, not about the trefoil.",
      "\u27e8c\u27e9_\u03b2 is a function of the BRAID WORD, not of the closure: the four words here present four different links, so this table on its own does not exhibit two representatives of one knot type. (The earlier note claiming \u03c3_1^3 and (\u03c3_1 \u03c3_2)^3 were two representatives of 3_1 was wrong on the topology \u2014 they are a split link and a 3-component torus link.)  The level ruling is what makes the datum well-defined: evaluate at the braid index.",
      "None of the values match the \u27e8c\u27e9 = 1 universal ansatz from the conjecture; the chiral case has word-specific structural values that are NOT given by the simple writhe-content formula.",
      "Combined with the deuteron empirical falsification (chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation.md:122-126), this demarcates the chiral residual of GAP-A-2: a structural formula relating \u27e8c\u27e9_\u03b2 to the braid topology is the open piece."
